.netlify/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately NOT ignored, and why
#
# AGENTS.md, .agents/, .claude/, .mcp.json, skills-lock.json and docs/ are all
# INTERNAL - no buyer should ever see them - and they are all TRACKED anyway.
#
# This template is the base every other ReUI template is cloned from, and the
# agent tooling is most of what makes cloning it worth anything. Gitignored, a
# clone would arrive with no MCP wiring, no skills and no docs scaffolding, and
# the next developer would set it all up by hand again.
#
# Keeping them out of the buyer ZIP is the packer's job, not git's:
# scripts/pack-template.sh in the reui-templates repo strips every one of these
# by name, whether or not git tracked them. That deny-list exists precisely
# because a .gitignore cannot be trusted for this - templates 1, 3 and 5 track
# their agent tooling too, and a clean `git archive` of any of them still
# contains it.
#
# Two exceptions, below: .claude/settings.local.json is per-developer state,
# and impeccable's engine binary is per-platform.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# impeccable's engine: a 12.7MB native binary built for one OS and CPU, so a
# committed copy is dead weight on every other machine and a new blob on every
# update. The launcher next to it (scripts/impeccable) fetches the binary for
# the current platform on first use, checks it against the release's .sha256,
# and caches it in ~/.impeccable/bin/<version>/.
.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/

